# playpick: mode=daily boss=flasks(unreachable -- see direction.md's
# driver-lesson note, a daily's boss is drawn from the UTC date, not a
# control on this screen) spec=hunter:marksmanship style=melee
# view=844x390,touch save=carried(behaves as fresh per #273)
#
# Probed first (2026-09-26-20-probe.play): today's actual daily is The Three
# Crowns, 25-player normal, SWARMING -- a boss this job has never actually
# fought (its two prior "crowns" appearances were both mode=walk, where the
# name is only a coverage label and the evening never reaches the room).
# Hunter has one spec, so its class tile just reads "Hunter" (class:15 in
# this grid) -- src/sim/classes.ts's specLabel drops the spec suffix when a
# class has only one, which is why marksmanship never appears as a choice.
#
# The point of this pull: hunter:marksmanship is a pure-ranged kit, and
# `melee` style has only ever been run against it once before, in a
# battleground (Ebb and Flow), where bill read hitsPerMin=0 for the whole
# match -- direction.md flagged that as worth a repeat against a real
# raid/daily pull rather than a battleground where the body kept dying.
open
tap daily
tap class:15
targets
ui
shot setup
tap start
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot open

play melee 80
bill
state
shot mid1

play melee 80
bill
state
shot mid2

play melee 60
bill
says
state
shot end
